## Program Outcome

Tool Shed moves deterministic Work1 and Work2 preparation and closeout into one thin resumable
runner while keeping semantic reasoning and authority with Codex/operator. The result is
behaviorally equivalent, failure-safe, portable, measurably reduces remedial interaction and
context, reports exact provider-measured remedial tokens with coverage plus separate GUI proxies,
and produces a sanitized per-project aggregate for the later IDEA-0007 dashboard.

## M1-CONTRACT-RESUME-SAFETY — Authority, state, and recovery contract

Status: complete
Depends on: none

Outcome: Freeze one public orchestration surface, exact phase/state contract, semantic and authority
boundary, skip classes, interruption/concurrency behavior, and bounded recovery/reporting rules.

Gates:

- `G1-ORCHESTRATION-AUTHORITY-CONTRACT-FROZEN`: the thin runner composes existing commands and cannot
  choose product behavior, evidence sufficiency, semantic version, deployment scope, or release.
- `G2-EXACT-RESUME-AND-FAILURE-SAFETY`: project identity, state/input digests, step evidence,
  mutation boundaries, duplicate runs, stale inputs, interruption, and current external evidence
  produce deterministic skip/resume/restart behavior without guessing or replay.

Candidate campaign: `freeze-scripted-orchestration-contract-and-resume-safety`.

Materialized campaign: CAMP-0127. Contract and resume-safety tests passed in the Work2 candidate.

## M2-WORK1-WORK2-KISS-SLICE — Compositional closeout runner

Status: complete
Depends on: M1

Outcome: Implement the smallest dry-run/resumable preparation and closeout runner for representative
Direct Work1 and Work2 paths, preserving independently callable underlying commands and exact
behavioral equivalence.

Gate:

- `G3-WORK1-WORK2-KISS-SLICE-QUALIFIED`: the slice composes identity/audit, work-level resolution,
  local view preparation, change-aware validation, outcome application, checkpoint/rebuild proof,
  Doctor, configured target verification, and endpoint-appropriate Git behavior without adding a
  second authority or automating semantic work.

Candidate campaign: `implement-and-qualify-work1-work2-closeout-runner`.

Materialized campaign: CAMP-0128. The compositional runner was dogfooded on this candidate and
resumed from exact phase evidence after a real generated-bytecode failure.

## M3-EFFICIENCY-REPORTING — Measured reduction and dashboard producer

Status: complete
Depends on: M2

Outcome: Establish an honest same-corpus baseline, compact result surfaces, bounded local telemetry,
and a deterministic sanitized per-project aggregate that IDEA-0007 can ingest later.

Gate:

- `G4-EFFICIENCY-OBSERVABILITY-AND-REPORTING-PROVEN`: deterministic orchestration is below 15 percent
  of measured execution interactions; known syntax, stale-view, and completed-step replay retries
  are zero; output/tool-call use materially falls; `remedial_tokens_actual` contains only exposed
  token deltas with `remedial_token_coverage`; GUI proxies remain separate; and the versioned
  aggregate excludes prompts, commands, paths, source, and granular activity.

Candidate campaign: `prove-orchestration-efficiency-and-dashboard-aggregate`.

Materialized campaign: CAMP-0129. The frozen same-corpus benchmark reports 8.0–8.7% deterministic
caller interactions, zero known retries, 39–40% interaction reduction, and 87–88% output reduction;
provider token totals remain coverage-labelled and separate from GUI proxies.

## M4-UPGRADE-RELEASE-RECONCILED — Portable rollout and closed loop

Status: active — Work2 checkpoint pending final target verification and cohort registration
Depends on: M3

Outcome: Prove fresh install, existing-client and maintainer upgrade, installed-skill synchronization,
provider-neutral fallback, reporting-schema compatibility/reset, rollback, supported platforms,
documentation parity, target behavior, release provenance, and final origin-to-product closure.

Gate:

- `G5-PORTABLE-UPGRADE-AND-CLOSED-LOOP-RELEASE`: all accepted requirements and authorized changes
  survive upgrade/rollback and are reconciled through current product truth and target evidence;
  IDEA-0011 closes without requiring hosted IDEA-0007 deployment or App Server availability.

Candidate campaign: `qualify-upgrade-release-and-reconcile-scripted-orchestration`.

Materialized campaign: CAMP-0130. Work2 owns implementation, local release-profile validation,
documentation-site build/deploy, focused target checks, candidate registration, logical checkpoint
and rebuild proof, and strict Doctor. Release, cross-platform exact-SHA CI, installed-client and
maintainer synchronization, rollback proof, and terminal upward reconciliation remain for Work5.

